# Forge's route search orders the quests of this guide and its guide writer writes the steps.
# Fixes go into data/route-fixes.json, data/guide-fixes.json or forever-db/corrections, never
# into this file.
# Added here: Wrongly Blamed, Justly Corrected (97250, Grunt Logmar in Camp Taurajo; its camp is a
# few steps east of Gann Stonespire; `when group 97250`: its Outraged Pillager is a level 23 elite).
# Further Instructions (1095) and Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle (1096): Sputtervalve's new orders go back to Ziz
# Fizziks, and Gerenzo (27) stands at the top of the Venture Co. tower on Windshear Crag, a short walk north
# of XT:4; both are on this guide's way up the Webwinder Path now that Ratchet comes first.
# Left out: The Harvester (897).
# Kaya's Alive (6401) comes from Makaba with Protect Kaya at the end of forever/horde/02-the-barrens and
# is handed to Tammra Windfield on the first Sun Rock stop, for players who carry it.
#
# Thunder Bluff first (0.3.6 bracket review, measured): Pigments for Paints (97538, Tah Winterhoof,
# 2100 XP: the Mirkweed grows in Mirkfallon Lake beside the Gaea Seeds' shore) and The Sacred Flame
# (1195-1197, Zangen Stonehoof then Rau Cliffrunner, 5490 XP: the phial from Ashenvale's Laughing
# Sisters at Raynewood and the moonwell south of it, the brazier in Splithoof Hold in Thousand
# Needles) are worked on forever/horde/07-ashenvale's walks and handed in on its Thunder Bluff and
# Freewind stops. The trip from Orgrimmar is a flight for Tauren and Paladins; the others fly to Camp
# Taurajo and walk up through Mulgore, and learn Thunder Bluff's flight path, which saves them the
# Mulgore walk on 07's Thunder Bluff stop. Everyone then flies to Camp Taurajo, where the southern
# Barrens begin. Druids take both quests at the end of forever/horde/06-hillsbrad-foothills, where they
# already train in Thunder Bluff.
#
# Shredding Machines (1068, Seereth Stonebreak, 1850 XP, needs Goblin Invaders from
# forever/horde/02-the-barrens): taken on the road west past Seereth, XT:9 and XT:4 east of Ziz
# Fizziks on the way up the Webwinder Path, handed in by players who come back past Seereth; its
# hand-in step shows only while it is ready.

# Horde 12-30 in the order the quest levels fit (2026-11-07): back from Hillsbrad at 24 for the
# Barrens' and Stonetalon's level 23-28 quests: the southern Barrens (Gann Stonespire, Blackthorn
# Ridge, Bael Modan) and the coast by Ratchet first, then Stonetalon: the Webwinder Path, Sun Rock
# Retreat and Stonetalon Peak. Their lower quests were done at 15-21 in forever/horde/02-the-barrens.
#
# Flow: Orgrimmar -> Thunder Bluff (Tah, Zangen) -> fly to Camp Taurajo (bind) -> Gann Stonespire,
# Bael Modan and Blackthorn Ridge -> Camp Taurajo (the hearth) -> fly to the Crossroads (Thork) -> fly to
# Ratchet (Sputtervalve: Further Instructions 1094 -> 1095; the Merchant Coast: Mahren, Isha Awak) ->
# back to the Crossroads (the flight the arrow picks) -> Seereth -> west into Stonetalon: Malaka'jin (Jin'Zil) -> up the Webwinder Path
# to Ziz Fizziks (1095, Gerenzo 1096), XT:9, XT:4 and Gerenzo's tower -> Ziz -> Sun Rock Retreat (flight
# path) -> Mirkfallon Lake and Stonetalon Peak -> Sun Rock -> the Charred Vale -> Sun Rock -> down to
# Malaka'jin (Jin'Zil). The next guide flies to Zoram'gar Outpost from the nearest flight master the
# player knows (the hearth to Camp Taurajo, or the walk to the Crossroads).
# Calling in the Reserves (5881, Maggran at Sun Rock, for Grish Longrunner at the Great Lift) and Message
# to Freewind Post (4542, Brave Moonhorn beside Grish) are done on forever/horde/07-ashenvale's way down
# the Great Lift into Thousand Needles.
#
# Hearth: bound at Camp Taurajo on the first stop there and used twice: from Gann back to Camp Taurajo, and at
# the end from Seereth's camp to Camp Taurajo for the next guide's flight. Sun Rock is not bound: its only
# use was the short way back from the Charred Vale.
#
# Rare-spawn quests (optional): Owatanka (884) and Washte Pawne (885) start from the drops of rare
# spawns: take them if you meet one.
#
# The Tear of the Moons (857) is a level 30 quest: General Twinbraid (30) and his Officers stand
# by the strongbox. It is taken at 28 in forever/horde/07-ashenvale, on the road from Camp
# Taurajo to the Great Lift (#1333).
#
# Carried on, finished: Trouble in the Deeps (6562, Je'neu at Zoram'gar, next guide) and Calling in the
# Reserves (5881, Grish at the Great Lift, next guide).
#
# Left out: Bloodfury Bloodline (6283, an elite harpy matriarch), Ordanus (1088, Alliance side of
# Ashenvale), Arachnophobia (6284, Besseleth is elite).
#
# Class quests: Shamans hand the red waterskin to Brine south of Camp Taurajo (Call of Water 1536)
# and take the blue one for Ashenvale (1534).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Thunder Bluff

step Fly to Thunder Bluff
  only Tauren,Skyborne
  zone Orgrimmar
  when !onquest 97538
  tip Fly to Thunder Bluff first: two of its elders give quests worked on this guide's and the next guide's walks.
  goto 45.3,63.7 "Orgrimmar flight master"
  fly "Thunder Bluff"

step Fly to Thunder Bluff
  only Paladin
  zone Orgrimmar
  when !onquest 97538
  tip Fly to Thunder Bluff first: two of its elders give quests worked on this guide's and the next guide's walks.
  goto 45.3,63.7 "Orgrimmar flight master"
  fly "Thunder Bluff"

step Fly to Camp Taurajo
  only Orc,Troll,Undead,Warrior,Hunter,Rogue,Priest,Shaman,Mage,Warlock,Druid
  zone Orgrimmar
  when !onquest 97538
  tip Thunder Bluff first: two of its elders give quests worked on this guide's and the next guide's walks. Fly to Camp Taurajo; from there it is a walk west into Mulgore and north to the bluffs, and Thunder Bluff's flight path brings you straight back to Camp Taurajo, where the southern Barrens begin.
  goto 45.3,63.7 "Orgrimmar flight master"
  fly "Camp Taurajo"

step To Thunder Bluff
  only Orc,Troll,Undead,Warrior,Hunter,Rogue,Priest,Shaman,Mage,Warlock,Druid
  zone Thunder Bluff
  when !onquest 97538
  tip From Camp Taurajo follow the road west through the gate into Mulgore, then north past Bloodhoof Village to Thunder Bluff; a lift at the foot of the bluffs takes you up.
  goto 47.0,49.8 "Thunder Bluff's central rise"

step Thunder Bluff
  zone Thunder Bluff
  when !onquest 97538
  tip Tal, the wind rider master, stands on the central rise: take his flight path if you don't have it. Tah Winterhoof and Zangen Stonehoof stand a short walk east of him.
  getfp "Thunder Bluff" npc 2995      -- Tal
  accept 97538                        -- Tah Winterhoof: the Mirkweed grows in Mirkfallon Lake, by Sun Rock
  accept 1195 optional                -- Zangen Stonehoof: the phial comes from Ashenvale, next guide

step Fly to Camp Taurajo
  tip Fly to Camp Taurajo: Tal on Thunder Bluff's central rise, or the Crossroads' wind rider master if you start this guide there.
  fly "Camp Taurajo"
  zone The Barrens

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The southern Barrens

step Camp Taurajo
  zone The Barrens
  tip The flight lands at Camp Taurajo's wind rider master. Tatternack Steelforge stands at the north edge of the camp, Jorn Skyseer and Mangletooth (in the cage) in the middle.
  accept 893                          -- Tatternack Steelforge, at the north edge of the camp
  accept 874                          -- Jorn Skyseer
  accept 879                          -- Mangletooth, in the cage
  sethome "Camp Taurajo"

step Grunt Logmar
  when group 97250
  tip Grunt Logmar stands by the flight master. His Outraged Pillager (23) is elite: grouping up is advised; the two Encroaching Soldiers are not.
  accept 97250                        -- Grunt Logmar: the soldiers and the pillager camp just east of Gann Stonespire, on the way south

step The Barrens
  only Shaman
  when onquest 1536
  zone The Barrens
  goto 43.4,77.4 "Brine"

step Brine
  zone The Barrens
  only Shaman
  tip Brine's hut stands on the ridge above the quilboar watering hole, south of Camp Taurajo, on the way to Bael Modan.
  turnin 1536                         -- Brine: the red waterskin from Tarren Mill
  accept 1534                         -- Brine: the blue waterskin is filled in Ashenvale, next guide

step Gann Stonespire
  tip Gann walks the road south toward Bael Modan, between about 46,75 and 46,81: if he isn't at the arrow, follow the road until you meet him. Sulhasa sits up in the tree just east of the road at 47.9,77.5.
  accept 843                          -- Gann Stonespire walks around Blackthorn Ridge: look inside the circle on the map
  accept 98093 @47.8,77.6             -- Sulhasa, up in the tree just east of Gann

step Wrongly Blamed, Justly Corrected
  when group 97250
  tip A few steps east of Sulhasa's tree, a small camp: two Encroaching Soldiers and the Outraged Pillager for Logmar. The Outraged Pillager is elite: grouping up is advised.
  kill 268622 quest 97250.1 @48.8,77.0
  kill 268623 quest 97250.2 @48.8,77.0

step Bael Modan
  tip South of Gann, the Bael'dun dwarves dig at Bael Modan. Excavators and Foremen work the pit; Prospector Khazgorm (26) carries the journal: pull him alone.
  tip Careful: Excavators (level 21-22) and Foremen (level 22-23) run off for help once they fall to 15% health, so more dwarves can join the fight.
  kill 3374 quest 843.1
  kill 3375 quest 843.2               -- Bael'dun Foreman walks around Bael Modan: look inside the circle on the map
  collect 5006 quest 843.3

step Blackthorn Ridge
  tip West of Gann, the Razormane hold Blackthorn Ridge. Kuz is on the east side, Nak to the south, Lok Orcbane at the west end. Lok (25) and the Warfrenzies (24-25) are a few levels above you; Hagg Taurenbane, a rare elite, sometimes walks the ridge: leave him. Pathfinders and Stalkers drop the Backstabber, Seers the Wand, Warfrenzies the War Shield. Washte Pawne, a rare red wind serpent, flies over the ridge: its feather starts a quest.
  tip Careful: Razormane Stalkers move around in stealth and hit with Sinister Strike, so they can join a fight without warning.
  collect 5073 quest 879.2
  collect 5092 quest 893.2
  collect 5094 quest 893.3
  collect 5072 quest 879.3
  collect 5103 optional               -- Washte Pawne's Feather
  accept 885 optional
  goto 42.5,81.0 "Blackthorn Ridge"
  collect 5093 quest 893.1
  collect 5074 quest 879.1

step Field to Clear
  tip On the way back east to Gann: Hecklefang Stalkers and Stormhide lizards roam the plain between the ridge and his camp. Careful: Qiraji Lieutenants (28, elite) sometimes stand on that plain: give them a wide berth.
  kill 4128 quest 98093.1             -- Hecklefang Stalker walks around Southern Barrens: look inside the circle on the map
  kill 3238 quest 98093.2             -- Stormhide

step Gann Stonespire
  turnin 843                          -- Gann Stonespire walks around Blackthorn Ridge: look inside the circle on the map
  accept 846
  turnin 98093 @47.8,77.6             -- Sulhasa

step Bael'dun fortress
  tip The Bael'dun Soldiers, Riflemen and Officers guard the fortress on the east side of the dig; all three items drop from them. General Twinbraid (30) and his Officers stand on the bottom floor: work the soldiers and riflemen on the upper levels and keep away from him.
  tip Careful: Riflemen (level 24-25) Shoot from 5-30 yd, so nearby ones can join a fight from range.
  collect 5017 quest 846.1
  collect 5018 quest 846.2
  collect 5019 quest 846.3

step Gann Stonespire
  turnin 846                          -- Gann Stonespire walks around Blackthorn Ridge: look inside the circle on the map
  accept 849

step The flying machine
  tip The dwarves' flying machine sits on its platform inside the dig site. Use the Explosive Stick of Gann that Gann gave you on it.
  interact 3644 quest 849.1

step Gann Stonespire
  turnin 849                          -- Gann Stonespire walks around Blackthorn Ridge: look inside the circle on the map

